[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64907,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrioid carcinoma of the vagina is a primary vaginal adenocarcinoma with histological features identical to those of endometrioid carcinoma of the endometrium.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64908,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8380/3 Endometrioid adenocarcinoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64909,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C71.0 &amp; XH0SD2 Adenocarcinoma of vagina &amp; Endometrioid adenocarcinoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64910,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64911,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64912,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>They most commonly occur in the upper vagina.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64913,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrioid carcinomas of the vagina predominantly occur in postmenopausal women, with a median patient age of 57&nbsp;years in the largest series {17895749}. Patients present with abnormal vaginal bleeding, or an asymptomatic mass is identified on examination. These tumours frequently occur in women who have had a prior hysterectomy for benign disease.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64914,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No epidemiological data are available.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64915,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most endometrioid carcinomas of the vagina arise in association with endometriosis or in women with a history of endometriosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64916,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64917,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is most commonly polypoid or papillary but may be flat, and tumours as large as 7&nbsp;cm have been reported. The cut surface is solid or solid and cystic.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64918,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The microscopic features are the same as those of endometrioid carcinomas elsewhere in the gynaecological tract, and many of the same variations in morphology seen at other sites have also been documented in the vagina, including squamous differentiation, mucinous differentiation, secretory change, small non-villous papillae, and the minimal deviation pattern {17895749}. Adjacent endometriosis may be seen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64919,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrioid adenocarcinoma is notable for its crowded clusters of cells with markedly increased N:C&nbsp;ratios and hyperchromatic, irregular nuclei that are smaller than those seen in endocervical adenocarcinoma. Large cytoplasmic vacuoles stuffed with neutrophils are also characteristic. However, none of the features are entirely specific.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64920,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64921,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p>The essential and desirable diagnostic criteria are similar to those in endometrium (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/223\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Endometrioid carcinoma of the uterine corpus</em>). The presence of endometriosis is supportive of the diagnosis.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T13:51:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64922,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The staging is the same as for other vaginal carcinomas.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64923,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 345,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Data are limited, but the prognosis is favourable overall. Outcome is related to stage, but recurrences of low-stage tumours have occurred.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:08:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]